#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-SD1365 expect=violation domain=SQDM
#note "Pins the SECOND Domains.Include token: 'SQDM' is 4 characters beginning 'SQ', which is exactly what SQ-- means (ScopeMatcher.firstMatchingDomainEntry, prefix+2 chars). Row 1 clean, row 2 has a population flag -> fires. Include matching is against the RAW dataset name, so the split-base path is not involved. FRESH - no twin equivalent; the SQ-- token is untested corpus-wide."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 QNAM=SAFFL
dataset SQDM label="Supplemental Qualifiers for DM"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col RDOMAIN  type=Char label="Related Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col IDVAR    type=Char label="Identifying Variable"
col IDVARVAL type=Char label="Identifying Variable Value"
col QNAM     type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Name"
col QLABEL   type=Char label="Qualifier Variable Label"
col QVAL     type=Char label="Data Value"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 |  |  | RACEOTH | Race, Other            | ASIAN-INDIAN
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 |  |  | SAFFL   | Safety Population Flag | Y
